# .cursorrules — dual CA + US (thepickleballcourt.ca / uspickleballcourt.com)

Persistent rules for every Cursor session in this repo. Canonical copies also live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (alwaysApply).

## Project
- Pickleball affiliate site built with **Astro**. Two indexable hosts from one repo:
  - Canada: https://thepickleballcourt.ca — `PUBLIC_SITE_REGION=ca`, tag `thepickleb050-20` (amazon.ca)
  - US: https://uspickleballcourt.com — `PUBLIC_SITE_REGION=us`, tag `uspickleball-20` (amazon.com)
- Cloudflare Pages: `the-pickleball-court-ca` (`build:ca`) and `the-pickleball-court` (`build:us`).
- Product source of truth: `src/data/gear.json`. Never duplicate product data elsewhere — reference products by ID.

## Architecture (do not break)
- `Layout.astro` — nav, canonical/OG/Twitter meta, Amazon disclosure footer.
- `ProductCard.astro` — product display + nofollow CTA.
- `index.astro` — homepage.
- `gear/[category].astro` — paddles / shoes / nets category pages.
- Articles live in `src/content/articles` (MDX, typed via content collection schema).
- Reusable UI in `src/components`. SEO helpers in `src/lib/seo.ts`.
- Extend existing files; do not rewrite from scratch. Keep existing routes working: `/`, `/gear/paddles`, `/gear/shoes`, `/gear/nets`, `/sitemap-index.xml`.

## Affiliate & compliance (hard rules)
1. Every Amazon URL MUST include `tag=uspickleball-20` (or the active `AFFILIATE_TAG` for the build region). Never emit one without it.
2. All affiliate links: `target="_blank"` and `rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"`. Route every affiliate link through `AffiliateButton.astro`.
3. Do NOT display prices as current/authoritative (Amazon Operating Agreement). Use "Check current price on Amazon" CTAs and price tiers ($/$$/$$$) or "as of" labeling — never a guaranteed live price.
4. FTC + Amazon disclosure on every page with affiliate links (top-of-body `Disclosure.astro` + footer).
5. Never fabricate prices, specs, weights, materials, ratings, or review counts. If missing, insert `{{ TODO: confirm }}` — do not guess or hallucinate.

## Content standards
- Original, genuinely useful, written for real pickleball players across all levels. No thin/spun filler, no keyword stuffing.
- Reference only products that exist in `gear.json`.
- Articles: clear H1, hierarchical H2/H3, fast-answer intro, comparison tables where useful, FAQ block (feeds FAQPage schema), pros/cons, ≥3 internal links + link to relevant category page.

## SEO
- Every page: unique title (≤60 chars), meta description (≤155 chars), canonical, OG + Twitter with per-page image.
- JSON-LD required: Article on articles, Product/Review where applicable, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList, site-wide Organization.
- Maintain internal linking and keep the sitemap complete after builds.

## Quality gates
- Run `npm run build` after every meaningful change. Never commit a red build.
- Semantic HTML, alt text on all images, WCAG AA contrast, keyboard navigable.
- Use Astro `<Image>` with explicit width/height to avoid layout shift; lazy-load below the fold.
- Mobile-first. Comparison tables must degrade gracefully on small screens.

## Commits
- Small, focused commits with conventional messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- List any `{{ TODO: confirm }}` items introduced in the PR/summary.
